        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
            "uid": "duckdb"
          },
          "format": 1,
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "-- NOAA GFS 10 m wind, u and v, for the next two days in ONE request: 17\n-- three-hourly steps of 53 x 51 = 2,703 cells, 45,951 rows.\n--\n-- Every other cell of the 0.5 degree archive, so one per degree -- a regular\n-- lattice, which both velocity layers need: they deduce the spacing from the\n-- coordinates and draw nothing if it wobbles.\n--\n-- Every step comes back, each row with its time, and the map's clock -- the bar\n-- at the bottom -- chooses which one is drawn: the latest inside its window.\n-- The dashboard's range, now-90m to now+90m, is that window when the map opens,\n-- so the step on show is the one nearest to now.\n--\n-- The request starts at the step at or before now - 90 minutes, so the window\n-- lies wholly inside the data. Started any later, kepler would clip the\n-- window's leading edge to the first step and leave it narrower than the three\n-- hours between steps, and a window that narrow, playing, spends stretches with\n-- no step inside it and draws nothing.\n--\n-- The window is written into the URL from `now()` itself, not from a variable:\n-- it stays the same URL for three hours, so ERDDAP answers every visitor after\n-- the first from its own cache, and no hidden variable rides along in shared\n-- links. `{0}` and `{1}` are `format`'s, not Grafana's.\n--\n-- `.csv0` has no header and no units row, so read_csv names by position. Only\n-- `[` and `]` need escaping (%5B/%5D). The two subscripts must be written\n-- identically or ERDDAP answers 400.\n--\n-- The cost is DuckDB's, twice over: it sends a HEAD before the GET, and ERDDAP\n-- builds the whole response for both. Measured at about 8 s once ERDDAP has the\n-- answer cached and 15 s before. `SET force_download` would halve it, but it\n-- outlives this query on a connection every dashboard shares, and would stop\n-- range requests into large Parquet elsewhere; `http_get` cannot send this URL\n-- at all -- it rewrites the query string, and ERDDAP answers 400.\nSELECT column0       AS time,\n       column1       AS latitude,\n       column2 - 360 AS longitude,  -- ERDDAP publishes longitude as 0..360\n       -- `u` and `v` are the names the velocity layers look for.\n       column3       AS u,\n       column4       AS v\nFROM read_csv(\n  format('https://pae-paha.pacioos.hawaii.edu/erddap/griddap/ncep_global.csv0?ugrd10m%5B({0}):1:({1})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D,vgrd10m%5B({0}):1:({1})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D',\n    strftime(time_bucket(INTERVAL 3 HOUR, (now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC') - INTERVAL 90 MINUTE),\n             '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'),\n    strftime(time_bucket(INTERVAL 3 HOUR, (now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC') - INTERVAL 90 MINUTE) + INTERVAL 48 HOUR,\n             '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')),\n  header = false,\n  columns = {'column0': 'TIMESTAMP', 'column1': 'DOUBLE', 'column2': 'DOUBLE',\n             'column3': 'DOUBLE', 'column4': 'DOUBLE'},\n  nullstr = 'NaN')\nWHERE column3 IS NOT NULL AND column4 IS NOT NULL\n",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Arrows on a screen grid over the flow field",
      "type": "ubica-keplergl-panel"
    },
